## Scope

The Java MessageQueueAssignment equals/hashCode mismatch remains runtime-local: its enum component uses Object.hashCode identity values, and the fixture constructs a collision for that JVM. This does not yield a stable cross-process HashSet bucket outcome; Rust retains lawful native Eq/Hash and exposes the stable Java equals behavior through java_equals.

Broad P18-V01 API, overload, input, error, control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation remains partial. Native Windows runtime and current-revision remote Ubuntu CI were not run. No push or remote CI was run. The four pre-existing Phase 19 worktree paths remain untouched and unstaged.
